## 3. User Roles and Permissions

Use the ERP's existing authenticated user and role system.

### Super Admin
- Create, edit, activate, and deactivate configurable fee structures.
- Configure fees for admission batches and seat categories.
- Apply fee changes to future admissions, selected batches, or selected students.
- Manage concessions and approve or perform financial corrections and reversals.
- View all fee records, payments, receipts, outstanding balances, and reports.
- Verify college-account bank transfers.
- Manage mess and hostel fee configurations and enrollment rules.
- View audit history.

### Principal
- View and edit fee configurations.
- Change individual fee components and apply bulk changes to selected batches or students.
- Manage student-specific concessions.
- View and edit fee records.
- Verify college-account bank transfers.
- View payments, receipts, outstanding balances, and reports.
- Perform authorized financial corrections and reversals.
- Manage mess and hostel enrollment and fee configurations.

### Secretary
- View and edit fee records and fee configurations.
- View and edit payment records as authorized.
- Verify college-account bank transfers.
- Manage and review development-fee collections, including payments made directly to the Secretary.
- View relevant receipts, outstanding balances, reports, and audit history.
- Perform authorized financial corrections and reversals.

### Office Accounts Staff
All accounts-related office users should be able to perform ordinary collection operations.

They can:
- View student fee records and outstanding balances.
- Record college-account cash collections.
- Record college-account bank-transfer payment requests.
- Record the student's initial bank transaction reference.
- Enter the passbook transaction number and verify bank transfers if their account has the appropriate accounts permission.
- Record development-fee payments and their supporting details.
- Generate and print provisional acknowledgements and authorized receipts.
- View payment history and collection reports required for their work.
- Manage collection records without changing fee rates.

They cannot:
- Change fee structures or fee component amounts.
- Change the assessed fees of a student.
- Create or approve concessions.
- Change a student's seat category to alter the payable amount.
- Approve their own financial corrections or reversals.
- Delete confirmed financial transactions.

### Departments
- No access to the Fees module, its APIs, fee records, student payment details, receipts, or financial reports.
- Enforce this restriction server-side.

Do not grant permissions based solely on a display name. Use the ERP's actual role and permission mechanism.

