## 10. Payment Categories and Destinations

Maintain two distinct collection destinations.

### A. College Account

College-account collections include the fee components payable to the college, including applicable college fees and mess/hostel charges.

Supported payment methods:
- Cash.
- Bank transfer.

### B. Secretary / Development Fee Account

Development fees are payable directly to the Secretary.

Track development-fee collections separately from college-account collections even when the student's overall fee assessment combines both amounts.

For development-fee payments:
- Online payments must record the transaction ID/reference supplied by the student.
- Cash payments must generate a separate numbered, printable development-fee receipt.
- Maintain the payment destination, amount, method, student, date, and receipt reference.
- Do not falsely represent development-fee collections as money deposited into the college bank account.

For Private and NRI structures where college and development fees are initially combined, support the correct accounting destination when the college configures the component breakdown. Do not invent an unsupported allocation.

