## 15. Payment Corrections, Reversals, and Refunds

Only Principal and Super Admin may perform authorized financial corrections or reversals, subject to their permissions.

- Never physically delete a confirmed payment to hide a mistake.
- Do not silently overwrite financial history.
- Preserve the original transaction.
- Record the correction/reversal as an auditable action.
- Require a reason.
- Record the actor, timestamp, original amount, corrected amount, and related payment/receipt.
- Ensure that balances are recalculated consistently.
- Prevent an ordinary office user from reversing, refunding, or changing a confirmed payment.
- Keep refund records distinguishable from ordinary collections.

The system must prevent corrections from creating duplicate payments or inconsistent outstanding balances.

