Record meaningful financial actions, including:
- Fee structure creation and edits.
- Bulk fee changes.
- Student assessment creation or authorized revision.
- Student seat-category changes affecting fees.
- Mess and hostel enrollment changes.
- Concessions.
- Payment creation.
- Bank-transfer verification or rejection.
- Receipt generation and status changes.
- Corrections, reversals, and refunds.
- Permission-denied attempts where appropriate.

Each audit event should identify:
- Acting user.
- Action.
- Affected record.
- Timestamp.
- Relevant before/after values where appropriate.
- Reason when required.

Never store plain-text passwords or unnecessary sensitive authentication data in logs.

